WEBVTT

00:56.131 --> 00:58.968
FILING FOR LOVE

02:24.136 --> 02:26.221
EPISODE 5:
HEART BURN

02:45.866 --> 02:47.242
Miss.

02:48.744 --> 02:50.204
My heart was burning.

02:52.373 --> 02:53.582
I'm ready to pay.

02:53.666 --> 02:55.042
SOJU

02:55.125 --> 02:56.585
Miss.

02:56.669 --> 02:58.212
You'll die if you drink all this.

02:59.213 --> 03:00.255
That's the plan.

03:00.339 --> 03:02.925
Did something bad happen?

03:09.515 --> 03:10.849
I don't know

03:12.101 --> 03:13.477
what's happening.

03:23.070 --> 03:26.448
Hey, are you okay?
You're alive in there, right?

03:27.241 --> 03:29.034
How many hours
do you need to shower for?

03:51.932 --> 03:53.726
You could end up getting dehydrated.

03:58.355 --> 03:59.648
I'd like a beer, too.

04:07.573 --> 04:09.366
Why are you so flushed?

04:10.075 --> 04:11.618
Are you unwell?

04:12.035 --> 04:13.036
Is it a fever?

04:14.079 --> 04:15.664
You don't feel hot.

04:19.752 --> 04:20.919
I shouldn't flirt.

04:21.920 --> 04:23.756
I can't have you falling for me.

04:25.132 --> 04:26.884
Can it really happen?

04:27.426 --> 04:29.011
Can you really fall for someone

04:29.303 --> 04:31.764
you've known for so long?
Like you were hit by lightning.

04:31.847 --> 04:33.348
Did you really fall for me?

04:33.432 --> 04:35.350
That's only possible
if I were struck by lightning.

04:38.645 --> 04:40.481
Of course, it's possible.

04:41.148 --> 04:44.276
If you're given a reason
to see the person in a new light.

04:44.860 --> 04:47.738
Or it's possible
you'd already fallen for them.

04:48.405 --> 04:51.450
Before you knew it,
all your built-up feelings about them

04:51.533 --> 04:55.120
just blow up in an instant

04:55.788 --> 04:56.914
like lava.

04:58.499 --> 04:59.833
Like lava.

05:01.210 --> 05:03.754
J CONVALESCENT HOSPITAL

05:09.092 --> 05:10.177
Mother.

05:12.679 --> 05:14.014
The people here.

05:15.265 --> 05:17.100
They're not harassing you.

05:18.435 --> 05:19.770
They want to help you.

05:21.522 --> 05:23.649
If you refuse your medicine
and cause a fuss

05:25.484 --> 05:27.194
they'll send you back
to the psych ward.

05:35.869 --> 05:38.080
FATHER

05:45.754 --> 05:47.005
- Hello, Father.
- Where are you?

05:48.173 --> 05:49.424
I'm exercising.

05:49.508 --> 05:51.760
You have time for that?
What are you up to?

05:52.219 --> 05:54.346
You hired a fool like that
for that much money?

05:54.805 --> 05:56.723
If you did,
you must've put him to good use!

05:56.807 --> 05:58.100
Why did you cause trouble?

05:58.976 --> 06:00.018
HAEMU FIRES LOCKETT
FOR SEXUAL MISCONDUCT

06:00.102 --> 06:01.228
The Audit Team went after him.

06:01.436 --> 06:03.438
You still don't have control
of your own people?

06:03.897 --> 06:05.983
Who do you take after
to be this weak?

06:06.191 --> 06:07.860
Think about who you are
and what you are.

06:08.026 --> 06:10.112
If you can't handle it,
you'll crumble, just like your mom.

06:28.547 --> 06:30.215
Starting today, I want Joo In-a

06:30.799 --> 06:32.050
included in the executive updates.

06:32.134 --> 06:33.677
The Audit Team
keeps tabs on executives

06:33.760 --> 06:36.555
and report regularly,
so the Head isn't included in...

06:40.392 --> 06:41.643
I understand, sir.

06:41.727 --> 06:43.896
We'll keep tabs on her ourselves.

07:12.966 --> 07:14.426
Hello, Ms. Joo.

07:15.093 --> 07:16.595
Yes, hello. How are you?

07:16.929 --> 07:19.264
It was a pity
you missed the team dinner.

07:19.598 --> 07:22.225
It was.
Let's hope there's a next time.

07:22.351 --> 07:23.393
How about

07:23.894 --> 07:26.146
you and I grab a drink?

07:26.229 --> 07:27.648
Just you and me.

07:30.859 --> 07:33.320
I don't see how you'd enjoy
joining me for a drink.

07:33.570 --> 07:34.738
We have nothing in common.

07:34.821 --> 07:36.531
There might be something.

07:36.907 --> 07:40.327
You and I could have
something surprising in common.

08:16.863 --> 08:18.115
Morning.

08:18.407 --> 08:21.118
Let's have a coffee.
We need to talk, too.

08:22.995 --> 08:24.079
Forget the coffee.

08:24.663 --> 08:26.456
We can talk in the interview room.

09:09.666 --> 09:11.877
- Yesterday...
- Sorry about that. I apologize.

09:12.961 --> 09:15.255
I shouldn't have done that
as your superior.

09:16.131 --> 09:17.883
If you want to lodge
an official complaint

09:18.592 --> 09:19.593
then go ahead.

09:20.052 --> 09:21.887
I'll admit and accept everything.

09:24.181 --> 09:26.391
You seem to be gravely mistaken.

09:27.601 --> 09:28.935
I kissed you.

09:30.687 --> 09:33.023
What are you talking about?
I'm the one who kissed you.

09:33.106 --> 09:35.317
I kissed you, Ms. Joo.

09:35.692 --> 09:37.235
Don't argue with me. I started it.

09:37.319 --> 09:39.571
I'm not arguing.
Do you think you used

09:39.654 --> 09:40.989
your rank or authority
to pressure me?

09:42.407 --> 09:44.910
Why are you trying to subdue me?

09:44.993 --> 09:46.870
- I'm saying I did what I did.
- I did it.

09:46.953 --> 09:48.955
- I did it.
- Why?

09:52.793 --> 09:54.377
Why did you kiss me?

09:55.378 --> 09:56.630
That is, if you did it.

09:59.758 --> 10:00.801
I was intoxicated

10:01.593 --> 10:02.677
with art.

10:03.095 --> 10:06.014
You're a great artist.
Your work was just beautiful.

10:06.098 --> 10:09.142
Not to mention the calm music
playing in the background.

10:09.226 --> 10:11.561
There was something about the moment
and its atmosphere.

10:12.229 --> 10:13.438
It was intoxicating.

10:13.730 --> 10:15.107
There's a scientific rationale.

10:15.190 --> 10:17.901
A great work of art
stimulates dopamine secretion

10:17.984 --> 10:20.821
which arouses you,
accelerating your pulse and breath.

10:22.906 --> 10:24.241
Like you're under a magic spell.

10:33.375 --> 10:35.001
Was what I drew that good?

10:35.794 --> 10:37.629
Do you think
I'm Michelangelo or something?

10:38.463 --> 10:40.549
I should call you Noh-chelangelo.

10:43.885 --> 10:46.096
The excuse you came up with
was that art intoxicated you?

10:46.221 --> 10:47.305
That's all there is to it?

10:48.932 --> 10:50.225
What about you, then?

10:50.475 --> 10:52.853
Why did you kiss me?
That is, if you did it first.

10:57.858 --> 10:58.942
You were pretty.

11:00.986 --> 11:03.196
I was stone-cold sober
and in my right mind.

11:04.030 --> 11:05.699
I just found you pretty.

11:08.451 --> 11:09.578
That's why I kissed you.

11:19.963 --> 11:21.131
I've always been pretty.

11:22.716 --> 11:24.593
Anyone would say so.
I have nice facial features

11:24.676 --> 11:26.052
and they're in the right place.

11:26.136 --> 11:27.262
I have an objectively pretty face.

11:27.679 --> 11:28.763
So what?

11:29.181 --> 11:31.516
That doesn't mean
every man kisses me.

11:37.522 --> 11:38.773
Regardless of who started it

11:39.274 --> 11:42.194
we have to admit what happened
yesterday wasn't normal.

11:42.986 --> 11:44.529
To make sure
this doesn't happen again

11:44.613 --> 11:47.324
let's keep a reasonable distance
for risk management purposes.

11:47.407 --> 11:49.826
We should keep our work
and private lives separate, too. Bye.

11:58.418 --> 12:01.087
Just so you know,
it's really annoying.

12:02.547 --> 12:03.798
Kissing and then apologizing for it.

12:11.264 --> 12:13.516
Mr. Cha, born in 1988,
Year of the Dragon.

12:13.600 --> 12:15.185
Your daily fortune says...

12:15.977 --> 12:18.772
Oh, you should organize
your surroundings.

12:18.855 --> 12:22.359
Hae-young, born in 1989,
Year of the Snake.

12:24.027 --> 12:26.655
Gosh. Someone special
will come from the west.

12:26.905 --> 12:28.365
- The west?
- Ms. Pyun.

12:28.657 --> 12:30.200
I live in Bucheon in the west.

12:30.992 --> 12:32.077
Am I special to you?

12:33.078 --> 12:35.914
Mr. Moo with the Year of the Ram.

12:37.123 --> 12:39.876
Try not to get noticed
by your superior.

12:39.960 --> 12:41.378
- My superior?
- Your superior.

12:43.922 --> 12:45.048
Where is she?

12:46.091 --> 12:47.926
- What's up?
- Shoot.

12:48.426 --> 12:50.887
Oh, dear, gosh.

12:51.263 --> 12:52.931
The economy has changed a great deal.

12:53.014 --> 12:55.392
What's the world coming to?

12:56.726 --> 12:59.145
What do you think is up
with those two this morning?

12:59.229 --> 13:01.523
Mr. Noh has always been
in Ms. Joo's bad books.

13:01.606 --> 13:04.192
I thought things had improved
while working on James's case.

13:04.276 --> 13:05.944
What if things
go really badly for Mr. Noh

13:06.444 --> 13:08.029
and chaos comes for him?

13:08.113 --> 13:11.741
I have a feeling we should step up
and help him out

13:11.825 --> 13:14.452
so the two can get closer.
Oh, my gosh.

13:14.536 --> 13:17.914
Oh, dear. AI.
Artificial Intelligence...

13:18.373 --> 13:19.374
It's just...

13:26.923 --> 13:28.508
I'm so jealous of him.

13:28.967 --> 13:30.760
This is his lucky year.

13:30.844 --> 13:34.389
He got married and was named
Haemu Cosmetics' King of Sales.

13:34.514 --> 13:36.891
It's not the first time
he won that title.

13:37.309 --> 13:38.643
The punk.

13:38.893 --> 13:41.479
I begged him to share
his trade secret, but he won't.

13:41.563 --> 13:44.065
- Let's go outside for a smoke.
- Sure.

14:07.839 --> 14:09.382
Are you all ready?

14:09.466 --> 14:11.926
One, two, three.

14:25.982 --> 14:27.275
What the heck's going on?

14:27.984 --> 14:29.027
What is she doing?

14:29.694 --> 14:30.737
Hands off me!

14:37.202 --> 14:40.538
I have no relationship whatsoever
with that woman.

14:41.206 --> 14:44.000
She's the head buyer
at one of our clients.

14:44.084 --> 14:45.835
I'm a salesman at her mercy.

14:45.919 --> 14:47.629
She's the buyer in control.

14:48.296 --> 14:49.381
That's it.

14:49.464 --> 14:52.759
But she caused a ruckus
at your wedding for no good reason?

14:52.842 --> 14:54.010
Exactly.

14:54.094 --> 14:56.596
How confused and rattled
do you think I was?

14:56.888 --> 14:59.766
If we had even a situationship,
I wouldn't have invited her.

14:59.849 --> 15:01.309
I'm not that crazy.

15:02.894 --> 15:04.479
Bros, this is totally unfair.

15:04.562 --> 15:06.648
We're not your bros, Mr. Do.

15:07.148 --> 15:09.734
Sit up straight.
We're not here to fool around.

15:10.068 --> 15:11.319
Sorry.

15:11.736 --> 15:13.696
Anyway,
there really isn't much to it.

15:14.614 --> 15:16.658
That's why even after that disaster
at my wedding

15:16.908 --> 15:18.451
I'm enjoying my newlywed life.

15:18.785 --> 15:21.663
There must be a reason she acted out.

15:22.163 --> 15:24.833
Did you give her reason to think
there was something between you?

15:28.711 --> 15:29.754
Well, actually...

15:30.588 --> 15:32.924
I've actually got
a sales tactic of my own.

15:34.300 --> 15:37.303
I sell lipsticks for a living.

15:37.512 --> 15:39.222
Most of the buyers are women.

15:39.305 --> 15:41.975
When a man and a woman work together

15:42.058 --> 15:44.269
there's bound to be
a little sexual chemistry.

15:44.352 --> 15:47.063
I use that as best I can
to make a sale.

15:47.397 --> 15:50.650
Are you saying you get your way
by using your physique somehow?

15:51.025 --> 15:54.112
Gosh, no, bro... Mr. Cha.

15:56.739 --> 15:58.616
Flirting. That's it.

15:58.867 --> 16:01.786
One, do just enough. Two, be polite.

16:01.870 --> 16:04.914
But how? You make the lady feel good.

16:05.373 --> 16:07.667
You create a thrill and tension.

16:07.750 --> 16:10.795
I prey on their emotions
without crossing the line.

16:11.754 --> 16:14.382
They usually know what's happening
and play along.

16:15.425 --> 16:18.011
Is Ms. So a bit delusional?

16:21.264 --> 16:22.974
We were definitely dating.

16:26.436 --> 16:29.522
You don't have to say,
"We're now officially together."

16:29.772 --> 16:32.108
There comes a moment
when you just know

16:32.525 --> 16:34.360
that you have something special.

16:34.486 --> 16:35.945
I was confused at first.

16:36.029 --> 16:39.032
I thought he was being nice
just to increase his sales.

16:46.372 --> 16:48.833
Oh, dear. Are you that ill?

16:48.917 --> 16:51.377
I said I was unwell, and he brought
porridge and medicine

16:51.461 --> 16:53.046
in the middle of the night.

16:53.922 --> 16:57.217
That's something you do
when you actually care about someone.

16:57.300 --> 16:58.551
Dress warmly.

16:58.635 --> 17:00.595
Yes, that's usually true.

17:00.678 --> 17:01.721
But in that case...

17:02.514 --> 17:05.308
I needed her to settle the bill,
and she said she was too sick.

17:05.892 --> 17:08.061
What else could I do
but try to make her feel better?

17:09.062 --> 17:12.273
I went to a nearby pharmacy
and bought all the strongest meds.

17:12.357 --> 17:14.234
- This must be taken warm.
- That, too?

17:14.317 --> 17:15.401
She loved the attention.

17:15.485 --> 17:17.946
- She wired the money the next day.
- Get well soon.

17:19.656 --> 17:22.200
So I accepted his date request.

17:23.201 --> 17:25.954
- Hello.
- We watched a movie and ate out.

17:26.371 --> 17:28.248
It was an ordinary weekend date.

17:29.040 --> 17:31.626
A date?
So that's what she thought it was.

17:33.294 --> 17:36.548
"I'm bored on weekends.
I roll around at home all day long."

17:36.631 --> 17:39.425
She kept whining, so I sent her
movie tickets the company gives us.

17:39.509 --> 17:41.135
When she got them...

17:41.886 --> 17:43.513
She said she was only free
that Saturday.

17:43.596 --> 17:46.641
It felt like I was going to work
on a weekend.

17:47.433 --> 17:48.768
"Going to work"?

17:49.561 --> 17:52.480
He never stopped saying
I was cute or pretty

17:53.189 --> 17:56.192
and wiped my lips
when I got food on my face.

17:57.318 --> 17:58.653
Is that part of his job description?

18:01.197 --> 18:02.323
Take a look.

18:04.367 --> 18:07.745
He texts me, "Good morning"
and "Good night"

18:07.829 --> 18:09.455
every single day without fail.

18:10.415 --> 18:11.916
And this means nothing?

18:12.834 --> 18:15.420
Let us take a look at that.

18:16.421 --> 18:17.672
Let's scroll up.

18:19.173 --> 18:20.800
OKAY, I'LL EMAIL IT TO YOU!

18:20.883 --> 18:22.135
GOOD NIGHT, SEE YOU TOMORROW

18:23.803 --> 18:25.179
I see your point.

18:26.889 --> 18:27.932
Thanks.

18:28.600 --> 18:30.059
The thing is...

18:31.102 --> 18:33.021
We checked Mr. Do's phone as well.

18:34.188 --> 18:36.899
He texts the same thing
to all his clients.

18:37.358 --> 18:39.527
It's practically copied and pasted.

18:41.070 --> 18:42.238
Copied and pasted?

18:43.948 --> 18:45.158
He's a psycho.

18:45.241 --> 18:48.536
Do you have another clearer incident

18:48.995 --> 18:52.081
that could help
prove your relationship?

18:55.335 --> 18:56.502
The kiss.

18:58.463 --> 19:00.298
He and I kissed.

19:01.341 --> 19:02.550
"Kiss"?

19:05.303 --> 19:07.805
This is just madness.

19:08.431 --> 19:11.225
I'm a guy who never crosses a line.

19:11.559 --> 19:13.436
Physical touch? Never.

19:13.519 --> 19:15.146
You brought her medicine at night

19:15.229 --> 19:16.898
went to a movie together
and texted each other

19:17.273 --> 19:20.109
- but you didn't kiss?
- We didn't. Never.

19:26.282 --> 19:28.534
Why did you stop the investigation
halfway through?

19:28.910 --> 19:31.162
You called a client over
for questioning

19:31.746 --> 19:33.206
and you don't conclude your report?

19:33.289 --> 19:35.917
It's a personal issue
between the two of them.

19:36.000 --> 19:38.294
They have different opinions
about one incident.

19:38.378 --> 19:40.129
How can we check that objectively?

19:40.630 --> 19:42.131
Don't you know the saying

19:42.215 --> 19:44.884
the truth between two people
isn't with just one

19:45.009 --> 19:46.678
but it exists
on the periphery of both.

19:46.761 --> 19:48.888
Then you must check the periphery.

19:48.971 --> 19:50.890
They clearly disagree on one matter.

19:50.973 --> 19:53.142
Ms. So says they kissed.
Mr. Do says they didn't.

19:53.226 --> 19:54.519
Isn't that an important point?

19:55.645 --> 19:58.147
If Mr. Do is denying kissing her

19:58.231 --> 20:01.150
that could be sexual harassment,
and it could hurt business ties.

20:01.275 --> 20:03.820
Not to mention
it's incredibly rude to the lady.

20:06.447 --> 20:07.782
I see.

20:08.616 --> 20:10.451
Is that how important a kiss is?

20:12.578 --> 20:13.913
Even after the kiss

20:15.498 --> 20:17.750
I thought an apology
would settle everything.

20:23.256 --> 20:24.674
Let's stick to work.

20:26.217 --> 20:27.427
Where did they kiss?

20:32.932 --> 20:34.684
It was after they ate here.

20:38.646 --> 20:40.648
Describe the situation in detail.

20:40.732 --> 20:42.900
Do your job properly, Mr. Noh.

20:55.204 --> 20:58.332
They left after having
a few cocktails at the bar upstairs.

20:58.416 --> 21:01.169
Ms. So can't drink much,
so she was very drunk.

21:01.252 --> 21:03.045
She could barely walk.

21:03.379 --> 21:04.547
And then...

21:16.058 --> 21:17.602
I feel dizzy.

21:19.061 --> 21:20.104
Oh, my gosh.

21:22.190 --> 21:25.735
So Mr. Do helped Ms. So
stand up straight.

21:29.530 --> 21:31.199
They stood here, facing each other.

21:47.298 --> 21:49.133
There's no need
to reenact the whole thing.

21:49.383 --> 21:50.927
You told me to go into detail.

21:51.010 --> 21:52.303
You're contradicting yourself.

21:55.932 --> 21:57.934
There's a camera up there.
Let's get the footage.

21:58.643 --> 22:00.186
It looks like a fake.

22:03.731 --> 22:04.732
How can you tell?

22:05.066 --> 22:06.108
Look carefully.

22:07.193 --> 22:09.195
There are no electrical wires

22:09.445 --> 22:10.613
or blinking light.

22:12.490 --> 22:13.825
It's cold to the touch.

22:14.283 --> 22:16.202
I bet it never worked.

22:16.619 --> 22:19.872
Hey, Mr. Noh. You have your uses.

22:27.588 --> 22:29.966
There should be a camera or two here.

22:37.807 --> 22:39.141
ROTISSERIE CHICKEN

22:49.461 --> 22:52.297
So, did the DOJ meeting happen?

22:53.256 --> 22:55.216
I heard JB pulled some strings.

22:55.300 --> 22:56.801
You jerk.

22:57.093 --> 22:59.762
You invited me out to practice
just to discuss work?

23:03.308 --> 23:06.561
Sir. It's Managing Director Jeon.
What shall I do?

23:06.644 --> 23:08.730
- Say I'll call him back.
- Yes, sir.

23:16.279 --> 23:18.406
Isn't she a looker? Can you focus?

23:18.490 --> 23:20.575
She's smart and thorough.

23:20.658 --> 23:21.993
You're so uptight.

23:22.076 --> 23:24.245
I understand.

23:24.621 --> 23:26.748
You need someone to talk to.

23:28.833 --> 23:31.920
I get that your marriage was
a business deal, but your wife...

23:33.671 --> 23:35.757
I couldn't live with her
even if my dad threatened to kill me.

23:41.846 --> 23:44.057
- Hello, sir.
- Hi there.

23:44.140 --> 23:45.892
The chicken looks amazing.

23:45.975 --> 23:49.062
They're so plump, I thought
they were turkeys from over there.

23:49.812 --> 23:51.356
They taste just as good, too.

23:51.439 --> 23:54.150
Mr. Noh. Isn't it mesmerizing
to watch them turn?

23:54.234 --> 23:56.736
I wish I could do that to you
whenever you get on my nerves.

23:57.695 --> 23:59.405
Oh, you like to truss people up?

24:02.700 --> 24:05.787
Sir, how many times a week
do you come here?

24:05.870 --> 24:07.914
I'm here every day apart from Sunday.

24:07.997 --> 24:09.249
Oh, really?

24:09.749 --> 24:14.087
Do you park your truck
at this angle whenever you're here?

24:15.421 --> 24:16.548
What?

24:16.631 --> 24:20.260
Do you park your truck
like this every time?

24:24.180 --> 24:26.474
It smells amazing.

24:26.558 --> 24:29.143
Take this home
and share with your family.

24:29.227 --> 24:30.436
You have a big family.

24:30.520 --> 24:33.106
We live separately now.

24:33.189 --> 24:35.108
Do you live on your own, then?

24:35.567 --> 24:36.609
Yes.

24:44.492 --> 24:45.577
Hello?

24:50.290 --> 24:51.833
You got the wrong number.

24:59.215 --> 25:00.508
Who was that?

25:01.259 --> 25:02.510
A wrong number.

25:03.928 --> 25:05.179
Let's take a look.

25:06.055 --> 25:07.765
We got the perfect angle.

25:07.849 --> 25:09.058
Press rewind.

25:09.601 --> 25:10.893
We must go back

25:11.603 --> 25:13.855
to between 10 p.m. and midnight.

25:16.733 --> 25:18.109
There they are.

25:40.465 --> 25:42.592
Gosh, they actually kissed.

25:54.687 --> 25:57.190
Mr. Choi got a call
that his second kid was hurt.

25:57.273 --> 25:58.650
I told him to go home.

25:58.733 --> 26:01.152
Good for you. Tell him to take
as long as he needs off work.

26:01.235 --> 26:02.445
Yes, sir.

26:03.112 --> 26:04.739
I'll drive you home tonight.

26:06.616 --> 26:08.701
It's fine. I'll drive.

26:14.082 --> 26:15.166
Bye, then.

26:19.545 --> 26:20.546
Ms. Park.

26:24.801 --> 26:26.094
Where did you move to?

26:45.655 --> 26:47.198
You can drop me off here.

26:54.706 --> 26:55.832
Thank you, sir.

26:57.458 --> 26:58.543
Ms. Park.

26:59.127 --> 27:00.753
From now on, Mr. Choi or Do-young

27:01.379 --> 27:03.172
will accompany me
on my personal business.

27:03.798 --> 27:06.384
I'd like you to concentrate
on work-related tasks.

27:11.180 --> 27:12.682
You don't have to do that

27:13.433 --> 27:16.352
if it's because my feelings
are making you uncomfortable.

27:19.439 --> 27:20.690
I live

27:21.607 --> 27:22.734
with a guy right now.

27:24.861 --> 27:26.529
He's a really nice guy.

27:28.030 --> 27:30.533
So there's no need for you to worry.

27:32.702 --> 27:34.912
I won't get all clingy.

27:40.793 --> 27:42.420
Speak of the devil.

27:43.755 --> 27:45.673
I'll see you tomorrow, sir.

28:02.315 --> 28:03.441
What's this about?

28:05.651 --> 28:06.736
Sorry.

28:07.487 --> 28:09.405
I used you for something.

28:09.489 --> 28:10.865
- Was that a guy?
- It's a secret.

28:11.407 --> 28:13.493
What do you want for dinner?
My treat.

28:13.993 --> 28:15.536
Why does everyone have a secret?

28:15.620 --> 28:18.372
- Who else has a secret?
- That's my secret, okay?

28:33.429 --> 28:36.057
Doesn't that clear up

28:36.432 --> 28:37.725
what our relationship was?

28:38.476 --> 28:40.853
Doesn't a kiss make it official?

28:41.854 --> 28:44.732
Do you two kiss someone
you're not dating?

28:45.149 --> 28:47.693
Am I the old-fashioned one here?

28:48.611 --> 28:52.156
I mean, if you kiss someone,
doesn't that mean

28:52.240 --> 28:56.202
you have a kind of relationship
that you should be responsible for?

28:56.536 --> 28:57.870
Yes, sure.

28:58.871 --> 29:01.541
But according to Mr. Do...

29:02.708 --> 29:04.001
We kissed?

29:05.378 --> 29:08.673
Now that I think about it,
maybe we did.

29:09.257 --> 29:10.758
I must've been too drunk.

29:11.592 --> 29:14.595
That could also mean
how insignificant it was to me.

29:15.096 --> 29:16.889
She wouldn't stop hitting on me

29:16.973 --> 29:18.391
so while we were drunk...

29:19.100 --> 29:20.309
You know what I mean.

29:23.688 --> 29:27.275
I'm old enough to know how things are

29:28.401 --> 29:29.610
and I'm not stupid.

29:30.278 --> 29:33.155
A momentary mistake
and an emotional connection?

29:33.239 --> 29:36.450
I can definitely make
the distinction very clearly.

29:39.412 --> 29:40.621
You're right.

29:41.831 --> 29:44.125
They're different. I'm not...

29:44.876 --> 29:47.169
You're not old-fashioned, Ms. So.

29:47.253 --> 29:50.047
We know enough
to be able to tell the difference.

29:50.131 --> 29:51.924
Yes, that's it.

29:52.425 --> 29:54.135
What, a mistake?

29:54.969 --> 29:57.763
He can't remember the kiss?
Does he have amnesia?

29:57.847 --> 29:59.849
Did the kiss happen
with only one person?

29:59.932 --> 30:01.309
Why is everything one-sided?

30:01.392 --> 30:03.561
I haven't made sense of it
at all yet.

30:03.644 --> 30:06.063
The other person concluded
like it was nothing.

30:06.147 --> 30:07.398
Right?

30:07.732 --> 30:10.484
So what? It doesn't change anything.

30:11.444 --> 30:13.613
Not all people who kiss are dating.

30:13.863 --> 30:16.365
In some countries,
a kiss is just a greeting.

30:17.158 --> 30:18.451
Do I have to

30:19.577 --> 30:21.329
marry someone just because we kissed?

30:25.082 --> 30:27.418
A kiss definitely makes it official.

30:28.628 --> 30:30.338
You kiss because you're dating

30:30.421 --> 30:31.923
and you date because you kissed.

30:32.298 --> 30:33.799
Our ancestors back in the day

30:33.883 --> 30:37.470
had to take responsibility
and marry someone they talked to.

30:37.553 --> 30:39.180
How far back in time are you going?

30:39.472 --> 30:42.433
These days, you sleep before you date
and go to bed first before going out.

30:42.725 --> 30:43.768
Sleep before what?

30:43.851 --> 30:45.978
You sleep with the partner first
before you start dating them.

30:46.354 --> 30:49.106
And you take someone to bed first
before taking them out.

30:50.524 --> 30:53.027
But aren't kisses a bit different?

30:53.235 --> 30:55.863
There's an old film
called Pretty Woman.

30:56.447 --> 30:58.240
In that film, Julia Roberts

30:58.324 --> 31:01.494
does just about everything
with Richard Gere

31:02.536 --> 31:05.164
but says,
"I don't kiss on the mouth."

31:06.040 --> 31:08.542
Why? Because kissing

31:08.626 --> 31:11.045
is more emotionally charged
than sleeping with someone.

31:11.712 --> 31:14.423
I don't particularly like Mr. Do

31:14.507 --> 31:16.759
but I believe
people can make drunken mistakes.

31:17.385 --> 31:22.098
I mean, getting physical
doesn't always equal a relationship.

31:22.181 --> 31:23.224
I don't know.

31:23.474 --> 31:25.351
We'll have to figure out
the situation before and after

31:25.434 --> 31:27.395
but what bothers me
is the fact that Mr. Do lied.

31:27.478 --> 31:31.148
It's the proof that shows
their kiss must've been significant.

31:31.232 --> 31:34.360
If it really meant nothing,
and he has a clear conscience

31:34.443 --> 31:35.486
he should've admitted to it.

31:36.237 --> 31:37.363
Hey, you're right.

31:37.989 --> 31:39.907
That's true. At times

31:40.616 --> 31:43.077
the truth is hidden between the lies.

31:44.787 --> 31:46.414
- Ms. Joo!
- Goodness.

31:47.873 --> 31:49.500
We put this together for you

31:49.583 --> 31:51.043
so make sure
you smooth things over with her.

31:51.127 --> 31:52.920
Kiss up to her and humor her.

31:53.004 --> 31:55.047
- Goodness. This way, please.
- You're all here.

31:57.174 --> 31:58.551
I'll just sit here.

31:58.634 --> 32:00.594
But I set up everything for you

32:00.678 --> 32:01.887
and warmed up the seat.

32:04.265 --> 32:06.100
I see. All right, then.

32:06.183 --> 32:07.560
This way, please.

32:13.190 --> 32:15.026
And a new glass for you.

32:15.109 --> 32:16.402
- Thank you.
- Sure.

32:20.865 --> 32:21.991
Mr. Noh.

32:22.491 --> 32:24.869
What are you waiting for?
She's here. Pour her a drink.

32:35.421 --> 32:37.757
What were you all chatting about?

32:37.840 --> 32:40.634
I saw a few of you
giving a whole speech as I walked in.

32:40.718 --> 32:42.136
It was this.

32:43.012 --> 32:46.015
Ms. Joo.
Kissing equals dating, right?

32:48.517 --> 32:49.518
What?

32:53.981 --> 32:55.024
What do you mean?

33:00.905 --> 33:03.365
You were talking about Mr. Do!

33:03.991 --> 33:07.161
Why are you discussing work
at a team dinner? You workaholics!

33:07.870 --> 33:09.705
Forget that.
Let's talk about something else.

33:09.789 --> 33:11.415
Why? It was just getting fun.

33:11.874 --> 33:14.543
It's not fun to talk about work
while drinking.

33:15.419 --> 33:18.047
- Now, why don't we make a toast?
- Sure.

33:18.130 --> 33:20.382
Fill up your glasses.

33:20.674 --> 33:22.176
Thank you.

33:22.259 --> 33:25.179
For the workaholics
of Audit Team Three.

33:25.262 --> 33:27.681
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

33:40.528 --> 33:42.738
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine. I'm okay.

33:43.322 --> 33:45.991
So do you want to grab
one more drink?

33:46.450 --> 33:49.620
Your team should let loose
without me in round two

33:49.703 --> 33:51.122
so you can talk behind my back.

33:51.205 --> 33:53.165
Goodness, don't say
something like that.

33:53.249 --> 33:56.210
All of us, especially Mr. Noh

33:56.293 --> 33:59.797
adore and respect you so much,
Ms. Joo.

33:59.880 --> 34:05.344
He's right. Ms. Joo, you are
the coolest boss in the world.

34:05.427 --> 34:06.720
He's drunk.

34:06.929 --> 34:08.180
Mr. Baek.

34:08.264 --> 34:10.558
You once said I wasn't good enough

34:10.641 --> 34:12.977
and that I should
draw the line for the team.

34:13.060 --> 34:15.938
Didn't you look at me like this
and get angry at me?

34:16.355 --> 34:19.608
Well, back then,
I didn't know any better.

34:19.692 --> 34:22.361
But Ms. Joo, you really know

34:22.444 --> 34:24.780
how to draw the perfect line!

34:29.034 --> 34:30.161
Mr. Noh.

34:30.536 --> 34:33.414
You should be good to Ms. Joo, okay?

34:35.541 --> 34:38.127
Goodness.
It's time for you to go home.

34:38.210 --> 34:39.503
- My gosh.
- Careful.

34:39.879 --> 34:42.590
All right, then.
We should call it a night.

34:42.673 --> 34:44.258
Okay. Wait, Mr. Noh.

34:44.341 --> 34:47.094
You should grab a cab for Ms. Joo.
It's quite late.

34:47.178 --> 34:49.096
- No, it's all right.
- It's not all right!

34:49.180 --> 34:51.098
Make sure you grab it for her.
Do that, okay?

34:51.182 --> 34:53.559
- See you tomorrow!
- See you tomorrow!

34:53.642 --> 34:56.520
- Sure. Have a safe trip back home.
- Mr. Moo.

34:57.771 --> 35:00.065
What? No, I can't do that.
It's too late.

35:00.149 --> 35:01.692
- The night is still young.
- No.

35:03.110 --> 35:05.196
They think I hate you, don't they?

35:06.488 --> 35:08.449
You have the best teammates.

35:09.408 --> 35:10.784
They're good people.

35:12.995 --> 35:14.205
So...

35:16.415 --> 35:17.875
it sounds like you don't hate me.

35:40.022 --> 35:42.191
Hey, there's my cab.
See you tomorrow.

35:44.109 --> 35:47.279
VACANT

35:49.490 --> 35:51.575
- To AL Tower, please.
- Sure.

35:57.915 --> 36:00.084
- Sir, please start driving.
- What are you doing?

36:03.045 --> 36:04.755
It's late, so I thought
I'd bring you home.

36:05.256 --> 36:06.924
You saw me get in the cab,
and that's good enough.

36:07.007 --> 36:08.300
And I had something to ask you.

36:14.765 --> 36:16.016
Did it really

36:18.185 --> 36:19.979
mean nothing to you?
Our kiss from that day?

36:23.232 --> 36:26.068
Don't read too much into it.
It was like an accident.

36:26.151 --> 36:28.654
So you want to let it slide
as if nothing had happened?

36:30.531 --> 36:32.783
What's with you, Mr. Noh?
This isn't your thing.

36:33.200 --> 36:35.119
You're acting like a teenage boy
who had his first kiss.

36:35.202 --> 36:36.578
I'm asking
because it wasn't my first kiss.

36:36.662 --> 36:37.746
I knew something was different.

36:41.333 --> 36:44.128
Then what? We kissed, so now we date?

36:44.670 --> 36:45.754
Do you want to date me?

36:47.464 --> 36:48.882
Let's figure it out.

36:49.133 --> 36:50.301
Let's find out

36:50.384 --> 36:53.095
if it was really
just a momentary impulse

36:54.513 --> 36:56.181
or if there's
something more between us.

36:56.765 --> 36:58.017
I want to find out.

37:03.022 --> 37:04.189
And how do we do that?

37:05.941 --> 37:08.319
Do you want to sleep with me? Do you?

37:09.695 --> 37:10.946
- What?
- Then get out.

37:11.572 --> 37:14.074
- Sir, we're here. Please stop.
- Sure.

37:22.166 --> 37:24.376
What are you waiting for?
Get out already.

37:27.087 --> 37:28.172
Ms. Joo.

37:34.470 --> 37:36.722
What's wrong? You wanted to find out.

37:39.183 --> 37:40.851
What if I really followed you?

37:50.944 --> 37:52.112
That's enough.

37:52.613 --> 37:56.158
I get what you're trying to say.
I'll try to play it off cool, too.

37:59.870 --> 38:01.372
Before I do that,
let me ask you this.

38:02.498 --> 38:05.334
Why are you pushing me away like this
after blowing my mind away

38:05.417 --> 38:07.294
with such a passionate kiss?

38:08.629 --> 38:11.048
Is it because
you don't like me all that much?

38:11.423 --> 38:13.884
Or is it because you're my boss
and I'm a part of your team

38:14.301 --> 38:15.594
which would
just complicate everything?

38:16.595 --> 38:17.763
Are those the reasons?

38:20.599 --> 38:21.683
If not

38:22.768 --> 38:24.228
then is there another man?

38:29.441 --> 38:30.526
In-a.

38:37.116 --> 38:38.283
In-a.

38:45.082 --> 38:46.333
I'm glad I got to see you.

38:50.254 --> 38:52.798
You changed your number, right?

38:53.632 --> 38:55.426
Why didn't you let me know?
I'm your father.

39:01.598 --> 39:03.434
How are you my father?

39:17.823 --> 39:19.783
You truly have become a stalker.

39:23.495 --> 39:25.164
I'm just worried.

39:25.622 --> 39:28.167
Who is that? Things seem cold.

39:30.419 --> 39:32.880
I heard you came back to Korea

39:33.672 --> 39:35.174
and wanted to see you.

39:37.426 --> 39:39.928
Where did you get that information?

39:41.305 --> 39:43.140
This is a serious breach
of personal information.

39:45.017 --> 39:46.185
Also

39:47.769 --> 39:50.522
since when have we met each other
and stayed in touch?

39:53.358 --> 39:54.359
I'm sorry.

39:56.361 --> 39:57.404
I have

39:58.822 --> 40:01.074
always left you alone, In-a.

40:02.326 --> 40:03.535
I feel

40:05.162 --> 40:06.788
really bad for doing that.

40:16.006 --> 40:17.841
That doesn't feel genuine.

40:20.594 --> 40:23.222
But if you really do feel bad

40:25.641 --> 40:27.893
why don't you
continue to leave me alone?

40:30.187 --> 40:32.648
If you call me
or come near my house again

40:33.106 --> 40:35.442
I'll report you to the police
as a stalker.

40:40.864 --> 40:42.324
Do not show up ever again.

40:45.202 --> 40:46.411
In-a.

41:08.767 --> 41:11.270
- That was great.
- Are you up for round three?

41:11.353 --> 41:14.356
- I know a place with hot girls.
- You're a newlywed.

41:14.439 --> 41:15.732
You need to go home early.

41:16.483 --> 41:19.027
My wife is having a team dinner.

41:19.236 --> 41:21.113
- Sure.
- I must enjoy the moment.

41:23.490 --> 41:24.658
And this freedom.

41:31.623 --> 41:32.874
She was that woman, right?

41:33.000 --> 41:34.459
The one who crashed your wedding.

41:34.585 --> 41:36.712
That's right.
My life almost got ruined.

41:36.795 --> 41:38.547
I was just humoring her
as a salesman.

41:38.630 --> 41:39.840
How did she read that much into it?

41:39.923 --> 41:41.383
But you kissed her.

41:42.801 --> 41:45.429
That was a drunken accident,
you punk.

41:45.512 --> 41:47.180
And is that a big deal?
Don't be old-fashioned.

41:47.264 --> 41:49.558
- Tell me.
- All right. Fine.

41:49.766 --> 41:51.018
So where are we going
for round three?

41:51.101 --> 41:52.686
- Your treat?
- My treat.

41:52.769 --> 41:55.147
- Hey, Mr. Do.
- Yes?

41:55.397 --> 41:57.691
Isn't that your wife?

42:00.319 --> 42:01.486
Hey!

42:01.903 --> 42:03.322
- Hey, Mr. Do!
- Mr. Do!

42:05.532 --> 42:07.868
- Hey!
- Hey! Stop it!

42:07.951 --> 42:09.244
- You!
- Min-woo!

42:10.287 --> 42:12.497
- You need to calm down.
- Let go of me!

42:12.581 --> 42:14.082
- That's enough!
- You.

42:14.166 --> 42:15.917
Who the heck are you?

42:16.001 --> 42:17.085
Stop it!

42:17.169 --> 42:20.339
That punk was kissing my wife!

42:20.881 --> 42:23.550
Would you be okay with that?
You'd lose your mind, too!

42:24.092 --> 42:26.720
- Is this true?
- Here's the thing.

42:26.803 --> 42:31.266
I had one too many drinks
at the team dinner.

42:32.017 --> 42:34.561
Also, isn't it kind of chilly today?

42:34.645 --> 42:36.688
So for a second

42:36.855 --> 42:38.982
I wanted to warm up my body.

42:39.066 --> 42:41.026
Listen to this girl.
She kissed because it was chilly.

42:41.526 --> 42:43.236
Are you still drunk?

42:43.320 --> 42:45.030
Then everyone out there
should've been kissing!

42:45.113 --> 42:48.700
Mr. Do, nothing is going on
between Ms. Lee and me.

42:48.784 --> 42:51.078
I admit that I made a mistake today

42:51.161 --> 42:53.914
but it was a drunken mistake,
and it didn't mean anything.

42:53.997 --> 42:56.291
Keep your mouth shut, please.

42:56.875 --> 42:59.294
Man, did you say
that kiss didn't mean anything?

42:59.378 --> 43:01.296
Then you can sleep together

43:01.380 --> 43:03.340
and even get married
without meaning anything.

43:03.507 --> 43:04.841
Unbelievable.

43:06.134 --> 43:07.678
You kissed my wife!

43:08.178 --> 43:11.014
- Hey! You have to stop!
- How dare you kiss my wife?

43:11.098 --> 43:12.891
- Why did you kiss her?
- Stop it!

43:12.974 --> 43:15.394
What do you mean
it didn't mean anything?

43:15.477 --> 43:17.020
- You punk!
- You have to stop!

43:24.736 --> 43:26.738
He was wearing a hospital bracelet.

43:26.947 --> 43:29.282
He was hospitalized
with a brain tumor.

43:29.700 --> 43:32.494
I had been worried
because he left without a word.

43:32.786 --> 43:35.038
His brain pressure
went up temporarily

43:35.414 --> 43:36.873
so he'll wake up soon.

43:37.791 --> 43:41.837
If I may ask, what is
your relationship to the patient?

43:47.175 --> 43:49.636
I'm his daughter, but not on paper.

43:49.720 --> 43:51.763
So he had a daughter?

43:51.847 --> 43:53.390
He didn't have any guardians

43:54.141 --> 43:57.686
and hadn't paid his hospital bills,
so there was quite a difficulty.

43:58.603 --> 44:00.731
I'm sure he had a wife and a son.

44:00.814 --> 44:03.525
We couldn't reach
any of his family members.

44:51.531 --> 44:54.785
HANEUN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

45:25.148 --> 45:28.443
Gosh, I'm sorry
you had to see all this, Mr. Noh.

45:32.697 --> 45:34.491
I'm not close to my father, either.

45:40.121 --> 45:41.498
I never had a chance.

45:42.415 --> 45:44.292
He passed away before I was born.

45:48.380 --> 45:50.006
But still, I had a happy childhood.

45:50.966 --> 45:54.261
My mom, two grandmothers

45:54.845 --> 45:56.596
great-aunt and aunt on my dad's side

45:57.556 --> 45:59.182
two aunts on my mom's side

45:59.975 --> 46:02.519
and my eldest, second,
and third sister

46:03.186 --> 46:04.813
adored me to death.

46:07.440 --> 46:09.192
You had a lot of women
in your life since childhood.

46:13.613 --> 46:15.699
I usually hung out with my sisters

46:17.033 --> 46:20.078
so I loved playing house
and playing with dolls

46:21.162 --> 46:22.747
but my mom hated it.

46:23.790 --> 46:26.376
Whenever she caught me
playing with dolls by myself

46:26.543 --> 46:28.169
she'd lash me harshly.

46:28.879 --> 46:32.257
Then I'd cry for getting lashed,
and she lashed me again for crying.

46:33.383 --> 46:34.718
She said that
men aren't supposed to cry.

46:36.761 --> 46:38.013
She must've been worried

46:40.056 --> 46:43.602
that she wasn't doing enough
to be both a mom and a dad.

46:44.352 --> 46:45.645
I'm sure.

46:48.565 --> 46:50.984
I understand everything now

46:51.985 --> 46:55.030
but something about that
must've left a scar inside me.

46:57.741 --> 46:59.242
This is a top secret.

47:01.036 --> 47:02.037
I still...

47:07.667 --> 47:09.836
sleep with a plushie.

47:16.468 --> 47:17.844
Keep it a secret.

47:19.554 --> 47:21.598
it's my first time
sharing this with another person.

47:22.223 --> 47:23.725
Thank you for sharing your secret

47:23.808 --> 47:26.561
thinking I'd feel embarrassed
about everything, Mr. Noh.

47:29.272 --> 47:30.774
It still feels like
I'm facing a bigger loss.

47:31.608 --> 47:33.276
It wouldn't be humane
to keep things exact.

47:36.321 --> 47:37.364
That's true.

47:54.965 --> 47:55.966
The first time

47:58.843 --> 48:00.845
I met my so-called father
must've been

48:01.846 --> 48:03.181
when I was seven.

48:05.016 --> 48:06.518
He was a married man.

48:32.544 --> 48:34.879
Have you lost your mind?
How dare you show up here?

48:35.588 --> 48:38.133
In-a, say hi to him. He's your dad.

48:38.675 --> 48:40.176
Hello.

48:42.470 --> 48:43.763
What are you trying to do?

48:43.847 --> 48:45.557
Is this your way of protesting
to get child support?

48:45.640 --> 48:47.976
You said you'd raise her on your own!

48:48.059 --> 48:49.811
You should get to meet her.
You're her dad.

48:49.894 --> 48:51.187
Stop saying I'm her dad!

48:52.105 --> 48:55.025
This neighborhood is tiny,
so once people start talking

48:55.108 --> 48:58.028
both you nor the kid
won't get to live an ordinary life.

48:58.862 --> 49:01.322
So just go. Darn it.

49:15.837 --> 49:17.380
He wasn't wrong.

49:19.424 --> 49:21.593
A scandal can be scary
in a small town.

49:21.676 --> 49:23.511
MOM AND DAUGHTER ON THE SIDE
AIRHEAD

49:24.095 --> 49:25.847
An adulteress
and her illegitimate child.

49:28.224 --> 49:30.351
We weren't entitled
to mourn over our misfortune.

49:38.485 --> 49:42.614
SUJEBI, BIBIMBAP

49:45.617 --> 49:47.660
"We must go somewhere
where no one knows us."

49:49.579 --> 49:50.830
That was the only thing on my mind.

49:52.123 --> 49:53.750
- Me too!
- I'm serious.

49:53.833 --> 49:55.251
In my case, I...

49:55.335 --> 49:57.170
Once I began to study
at a university in Seoul

49:57.962 --> 50:00.465
I finally thought
I had a chance at an ordinary life.

50:01.508 --> 50:02.884
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

50:05.303 --> 50:07.472
- It's so good.
- Yes, it's really good.

50:10.350 --> 50:11.768
Mom!

50:14.354 --> 50:15.522
Are you going to work?

50:16.064 --> 50:17.440
Bye!

50:23.321 --> 50:25.406
- She's your mom?
- Yes.

50:26.616 --> 50:29.119
- No way.
- What's up?

50:30.411 --> 50:34.165
Have you really been doing this?
What now? A nude model?

50:35.416 --> 50:37.043
This is crazy.

50:37.127 --> 50:39.087
I saw the job ad by chance

50:40.380 --> 50:43.550
and started doing it
because it paid more than other jobs.

50:45.009 --> 50:47.137
I really don't understand, Mom.

50:47.720 --> 50:50.723
It doesn't matter
how much you're paid.

50:50.807 --> 50:52.976
Ordinary people
don't pick up a job like this.

50:56.437 --> 50:57.689
It's freeing.

50:59.149 --> 51:00.150
What?

51:00.984 --> 51:02.944
I feel free

51:05.822 --> 51:07.782
while I stand there.

51:08.825 --> 51:11.828
And I begin...

51:14.664 --> 51:15.748
to like myself

51:16.916 --> 51:18.626
for the first time in my life.

51:20.336 --> 51:21.588
So you're saying

51:22.297 --> 51:25.508
you felt free while standing naked
in front of others?

51:27.010 --> 51:29.095
Shouldn't it be shameful
and embarrassing?

51:30.597 --> 51:32.265
I had always pitied you.

51:32.348 --> 51:35.310
I believed that you dated Dad
without knowing he was married.

51:35.393 --> 51:37.687
I didn't care what others said.
I said your slate was clean!

51:39.355 --> 51:40.398
But you know what?

51:40.899 --> 51:42.817
Maybe it is true, Mom.

51:43.902 --> 51:44.986
You are that woman.

51:52.118 --> 51:53.453
I'm leaving this place.

51:53.912 --> 51:55.872
- In-a.
- I realized

51:55.955 --> 51:59.209
there is only one way to escape

51:59.584 --> 52:01.211
from this sickening scarlet letter.

52:01.920 --> 52:03.296
Not living as your daughter.

52:37.664 --> 52:40.917
INCOMING CALL

52:43.211 --> 52:44.545
Hello?

52:44.629 --> 52:46.798
Hello, I am Lieutenant Yoon Ha-jun
with Nambu Police Station.

52:47.173 --> 52:48.883
Are you
Ms. Joo Kyeong-hee's daughter?

52:56.808 --> 52:59.394
She got into an accident
at Sillim Intersection.

53:01.020 --> 53:03.273
She must've been there
to visit you at your place.

53:04.232 --> 53:07.944
She was on her way home
after waiting outside until late.

53:22.667 --> 53:26.254
CONTACTS

53:26.337 --> 53:27.714
WORK

53:27.797 --> 53:29.841
MY DAUGHTER IN-A

53:29.924 --> 53:30.967
ART CLASS

53:41.185 --> 53:43.479
ART CLASS

53:46.149 --> 53:47.358
Hello?

53:47.442 --> 53:50.987
Ms. Kyeong-hee, are you coming
to the class on Friday?

53:51.738 --> 53:54.073
You haven't picked up,
so I've been worried.

55:16.280 --> 55:17.490
I finally understood

55:18.533 --> 55:19.951
what my mom said.

55:21.536 --> 55:23.704
I understood what it was like
to throw myself as is

55:25.415 --> 55:27.667
into the world
that doesn't hold a prejudice.

55:29.127 --> 55:30.670
Then I realized

55:31.337 --> 55:32.839
I had never

55:35.633 --> 55:36.884
forgiven my mom

55:39.720 --> 55:41.180
or my existence

55:42.515 --> 55:44.475
in my life.

55:56.988 --> 55:57.989
Are you crying?

55:59.157 --> 56:01.325
Wait, why are you crying?
Are you drunk?

56:02.118 --> 56:04.370
- Have a cup of water.
- It's heartbreaking.

56:12.503 --> 56:14.130
You must've been very lonely.

56:25.433 --> 56:27.143
You keep acting tough

56:29.770 --> 56:30.980
which is making it worse.

56:36.861 --> 56:38.654
You little...

56:56.839 --> 56:58.174
Please stop hurting.

57:02.970 --> 57:05.681
You're the worst drunk.

58:12.957 --> 58:15.084
Mr. Noh, you're home.

58:15.167 --> 58:16.502
Get up. Hey.

58:17.628 --> 58:18.838
Mr. Noh.

58:18.921 --> 58:20.965
Mr. Noh, get up. You're home.

58:22.633 --> 58:24.427
Mr. Noh!

58:27.138 --> 58:29.056
I'm sorry. We'll get off now.

58:32.685 --> 58:33.936
Get over here.

58:51.245 --> 58:52.663
NOH KI-JUN
AUDIT TEAM 3

58:53.581 --> 58:55.416
Block 101, Unit 1002?

59:05.885 --> 59:07.261
Well, he's not going
to freeze to death.

59:11.891 --> 59:13.225
Jeez.

59:15.561 --> 59:16.854
We'll have a talk tomorrow.

59:17.480 --> 59:19.815
I will use all of my status
and authority

59:21.108 --> 59:23.861
and make you pay for this.

59:29.450 --> 59:30.576
You're so heavy.

59:41.712 --> 59:45.424
Mr. Noh, will you wake up? Please!

59:48.761 --> 59:51.222
I'm sure
your unconscious mind remembers.

59:51.305 --> 59:54.642
Press the code. Here. Do it.

01:00:14.412 --> 01:00:17.331
FILING FOR LOVE

01:00:17.915 --> 01:00:20.710
GUEST APPEARANCE
BY HWANG HEE AND KIM YE-WON

01:00:45.443 --> 01:00:46.610
How are you feeling, Ms. Joo?

01:00:46.694 --> 01:00:48.612
What is this, Ki-jun?

01:00:48.696 --> 01:00:50.948
Is there a reason
why Joo In-a can't find out

01:00:51.031 --> 01:00:52.032
about our relationship?

01:00:52.700 --> 01:00:53.909
It's your personal life.

01:00:53.993 --> 01:00:55.786
Something like this cannot...

01:00:55.870 --> 01:00:56.996
I said, cannot distract me.

01:00:57.079 --> 01:00:58.706
Do you not care
about my personal life?

01:00:59.749 --> 01:01:01.000
You even kissed me.

01:01:01.667 --> 01:01:04.295
Stop feigning ignorance.
You already know.

01:01:04.712 --> 01:01:06.756
About your question, Mr. Noh...

01:01:06.839 --> 01:01:09.008
The real reason
why I keep pushing you away...

01:01:09.633 --> 01:01:10.885
I...

01:01:10.968 --> 01:01:12.011
Ms. Joo!

01:01:13.637 --> 01:01:15.264
I've lost a bit of my mind

01:01:15.723 --> 01:01:16.932
because of you.

01:01:29.945 --> 01:01:31.947
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
